-- title:
--   Tame inertia acts on the Drinfeld chart by diag(d,1)
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic data. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of level $\{q\ell\}$, let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity.
--
--   Function field and integral base. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which, by the hypothesis `hK`, is the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), the level group being the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q\in\mathfrak{m}_A$ and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A\to L$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A\to L\to K$. Let $j\in K$ be non-zero with Laurent expansion the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant, and let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$.
--
--   Geometric point. Let $X=\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$, the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$, respectively $A[j^{-1}]$, in $K$ along their common mid chart. Let $z$ be a point of $X$, let $\varpi z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ along the structure morphism `TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase` (hypothesis `hϖz`), and assume $\varpi z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$. Let $y$ be a point of `XFin`$=\operatorname{Spec}$ of the chart algebra $R:=$`chartAlgFin A K j` (the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$) with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y)=z$. The hypothesis `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:R\to\Omega$ whose kernel is the prime $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is: every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Chart witness. Let $W$ be a discrete valuation domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal, let $\sigma:A\to W$ be a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak{m}_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, and let $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$ (the form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)). Put $S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma\varpi)v-fu)$ with quotient map $\mathrm{mk}_S$, let $\mathrm{toC}$ be the map from $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ to its $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion, and let $e$ be a ring isomorphism from that completion onto $S$. Write $\mathrm{germY}:R\to\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ for the composite of the canonical identification of $R$ with the sections of `XFin` over $\top$, the inverse of the comparison isomorphism for $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$, and the germ map at $z$ on the open image of $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$.
--
--   Three clauses on the witness are assumed. `hconst`: for every $a\in A$, $e$ carries the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ of $a$ (along `toBase`) to $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma a))$. `hlin` (level equivariance): for every $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is, for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g$ having non-zero Laurent series, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and every embedding $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, one has $\iota_*\big((\tau x)\big)\cdot q\text{-}\exp(g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell,\gamma^{-1}))=q\text{-}\exp(f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell,\gamma^{-1}))$ — and every proof `hpres` that $\tau$ maps $R$ into $R$, if the induced endomorphism of $R$ satisfies $\tau a-a\in y$ for all $a\in R$, then there are $\theta:S\cong S$, $c\in W$ and $M\in M_2(W)$ such that $\theta\circ e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}=e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}\circ\tau$ on $R$; $\theta$ fixes every $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(w))$; $\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S X_{j})-\mathrm{mk}_S\big(\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i\big)\in(\mathrm{mk}_SX_0,\mathrm{mk}_SX_1)^2$ for each $j$; $c^{q+1}-1\in\mathfrak{m}_W$; $M_{ij}-c\,\gamma_{ij}\in\mathfrak{m}_W$ for all $i,j$; $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ implies $c-1\in\mathfrak{m}_W$; and if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ then $c-1\notin\mathfrak{m}_W$. `hanchor` (branch anchoring): for every prime ideal $P$ of $S$ not containing both $\mathrm{mk}_SX_0$ and $\mathrm{mk}_SX_1$, containing $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma\varpi))$, and containing an element $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(1)X_0+C(0)X_1+h)$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and for every $a\in R$: $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ lies in the preimage of $P$ under $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ in $L((t))$ is the image of an element of $\mathfrak{m}_A$.
--
--   Conclusion. Under these hypotheses the following holds. Let $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, and let $\sigma_L$ be a ring automorphism of $L$ and $\sigma_A$ a ring automorphism of $A$ such that $\sigma_L$ and $\sigma_A$ agree through $A\to L$, such that $\sigma_A a-a\in\mathfrak{m}_A$ for every $a\in A$, and such that $\sigma_L\zeta=\zeta^{v}$ where $v$ is the natural-number representative of $d$ in $\mathbb{Z}/q$. Let $\tau$ be a ring automorphism of $K$ acting on Laurent expansions coefficientwise by $\sigma_L$, such that $\tau$ maps $R$ into $R$ (by a proof `hpres` used below), such that $\tau^{-1}$ maps $R$ into $R$, and such that the induced endomorphism of $R$ satisfies $\tau a-a\in y$ for all $a\in R$. Let $\theta:S\cong S$ and $\sigma_W:W\cong W$ satisfy: $\theta(e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))))=e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\tau a)))$ for all $a\in R$; $\sigma_W\circ\sigma=\sigma\circ\sigma_A$ on $A$; $\sigma_W w-w\in\mathfrak{m}_W$ for all $w\in W$; and $\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S(C(w)))=\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_W w))$ for all $w\in W$. Then there exists a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with the following two properties.
--
--   First, $M$ is a linear part of $\theta$: for each $j\in\{0,1\}$,
--   $$\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S X_j)-\mathrm{mk}_S\Big(\sum_{i} C(M_{ij})X_i\Big)\in\big(\mathrm{mk}_SX_0,\mathrm{mk}_SX_1\big)^2 .$$
--
--   Second, modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ this linear part is the prescribed diagonal matrix: for all $i,j\in\{0,1\}$,
--   $$M_{ij}-\Big(\big(d\cdot \mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^q)^{-1}\big)_{ij}\Big)^{\!\sim}\in\mathfrak{m}_W,$$
--   where [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.diagOneElem q (d^q)⁻¹`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L233) is the element $\mathrm{diag}(1,(d^q)^{-1})$ of $GL_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$, the product is the scalar multiple of its underlying matrix by $d\in\mathbb{Z}/q$, and $(\cdot)^{\sim}$ denotes the image in $W$ of the natural-number representative of an element of $\mathbb{Z}/q$. Since $d^{q-1}=1$, this matrix is $\mathrm{diag}(d,1)$.
--
--   This is the computation of the linear part of the action of an inertia element at $q$, with cyclotomic character value $d$, on a Drinfeld chart at a supersingular point of the integral model of the modular curve of level $H_1$: for any semilinear automorphism $\theta$ of the chart induced by such an inertia element the reduction of its linear part is $\mathrm{diag}(d,1)$. It is the input for [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.inertia_drinfeldChart_semilinear_linearPart_diagOneElem_of_linearPart_riders_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.inertia_drinfeldChart_semilinear_linearPart_diagOneElem_of_linearPart_riders_twoChartIntegralModel), where it is combined with the remaining clauses on the chart witness.
